{"absent":["Memory layout and size of the 64-bit and long atomic containers","Machine mechanism providing indivisibility in the lower raw primitives","Exact boolean outcome encoding of test and conditional-update services","Whether failed conditional updates still emit access marks or barriers","Futex, spinlock, mutex, semaphore, and other blocking synchronization behavior","Lock ordering, interrupt context, and preemption rules for these operations"],"dossier":"D03","findings":[{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_xchg_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_xchg_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_xchg_relaxed"],"text":"Instrumented 64-bit exchange service offers ordering-specific entry points that atomically replace the stored value and report the predecessor. Ordering strength is selected by name suffix."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_cmpxchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_cmpxchg_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_cmpxchg_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_cmpxchg_relaxed"],"text":"Instrumented 64-bit compare exchange service offers default plus ordering-specific entries that conditionally store a successor only when current contents equal an expected value and report the observed predecessor."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_try_cmpxchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_try_cmpxchg_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_try_cmpxchg_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_try_cmpxchg_relaxed"],"text":"Instrumented boolean-style compare exchange service accepts a caller-owned expected-value cell alongside the target and successor, allowing the expected cell to participate in the outcome contract with default and ordering-specific variants."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_sub_and_test","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_dec_and_test","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_inc_and_test","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_add_negative","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_add_negative_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_add_negative_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_add_negative_relaxed"],"text":"Instrumented 64-bit arithmetic test services combine an update with a predicate result, covering subtract, decrement, increment, and signed-negativity checks, with negativity checks also exposed in ordering-specific forms."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_fetch_add_unless","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_add_unless","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_inc_not_zero","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_inc_unless_negative","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_dec_unless_positive","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_dec_if_positive"],"text":"Instrumented 64-bit conditional update services suppress modification when a named guard holds, covering exclusion of one sentinel value and zero, sign, and positivity guards for increment and decrement."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_read","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_read_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_set","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_set_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_add_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_fetch_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_sub","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_sub_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_fetch_sub","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_inc","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_inc_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_fetch_inc","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_dec","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_dec_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_fetch_dec"],"text":"Width-abstracted long front layer exposes reads, stores, and arithmetic updates with return-new, return-old, plain, and ordering-specific shapes, hiding whether the native word is 32 or 64 bits."},{"kind":"export","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_read","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_read_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_set","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_set_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_add_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_fetch_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_sub","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_inc","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_fetch_inc","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_dec","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_fetch_dec"],"text":"Bare long adaptation layer forwards each long operation to the same-shaped fixed-width primitive for the configured word size, preserving operation family and ordering suffix."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_xchg_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_xchg_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_cmpxchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_cmpxchg_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_add_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_add_return_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_add_return_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_add_return_relaxed"],"text":"Concurrency-marker pairing is fixed by ordering: default full-strength entries carry the full barrier marker, release entries carry the release marker, while acquire and relaxed entries carry no such marker."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_try_cmpxchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_cmpxchg","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_read","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_set","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_fetch_add"],"text":"Access marking distinguishes operation effect: pure loads mark read, pure stores mark write, read-modify-write entries mark read-write over the whole target, and boolean compare exchange additionally marks its expected-value cell for read-write."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_read","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_set","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_add_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_fetch_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_sub_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_inc_return","include/linux/atomic/atomic-long.h::raw_atomic_long_dec_return"],"text":"Word-size selection is a compile-time choice: 64-bit builds use the 64-bit fixed-width counterpart and other builds use the narrower counterpart, with identical arity and result forwarding."},{"kind":"invariant","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_xchg_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_cmpxchg_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_add","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_inc","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_dec"],"text":"These wrappers add only checking and marking around delegation; they establish no mutual exclusion themselves and inherit atomicity and visibility from the lower raw primitives they invoke."},{"kind":"hazard","sids":["include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_add_negative_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_add_negative_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic64_add_negative_relaxed","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_fetch_add_acquire","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_fetch_add_release","include/linux/atomic/atomic-instrumented.h::atomic_long_fetch_add_relaxed"],"text":"Substituting one ordering suffix for another changes the associated checking marker and the delegated primitive, so an incorrect suffix silently weakens or strengthens the intended cross-thread visibility contract."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/instrumented.h::instrument_atomic_read_write"],"text":"External read-write access-marking helper relied upon by instrumented wrappers."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/kcsan-checks.h::kcsan_mb.alt_1"],"text":"External full-barrier concurrency marker relied upon by default-strength wrappers."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/kcsan-checks.h::kcsan_mb.alt_3"],"text":"External full-barrier concurrency marker relied upon by default-strength wrappers."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/kcsan-checks.h::kcsan_release.alt_1"],"text":"External release concurrency marker relied upon by release-strength wrappers."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/kcsan-checks.h::kcsan_release.alt_3"],"text":"External release concurrency marker relied upon by release-strength wrappers."},{"kind":"stub","sids":["include/linux/instrumented.h::instrument_read